==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{unk|ru}}:
* Often interpreted as inherited from {{inh|ru|orv|*очьнь}} from {{m|orv|око||eye}}; the semantic shift might be "visibly > obviously > prominently > very". The non-productive ending is similar to adverbs like {{m|ru|вкривь}}, {{m|ru|впрямь}}, {{m|ru|встарь}}.
* Alternatively, proposed by Lehrman (1987) to be a borrowing from a {{bor|ru|urj-fin|-}} language. Compare {{ncog|fi|oikein}} and {{ncog|izh|oikiin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|о́чень}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-очень.ogg}}

===Adverb===
{{ru-adv|о́чень}}

# [[very]], [[really]], [[much]], very much
#: {{syn|ru|изря́дно|весьма́|дю́же}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[такое|Тако́е]] [[случа́ется]] '''о́чень''' [[ре́дко]].|This happens '''very''' rarely.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''о́чень''' [[люблю́]] [[тебя́]].|I '''really''' love you. / I love you '''very much'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] '''о́чень''' [[тру́дно]].|It's '''really''' hard.}}

===Predicative===
{{head|ru|predicative|head=о́чень}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial|in the negative}} not [[very]] [[good]], not [[very]] [[well]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[всё|Всё]] [[прошло́]] [[не]] '''о́чень'''.|It didn't go '''very well'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[дела|Дела́]] [[иду́т]] [[не]] '''о́чень'''.|Things aren't going '''very well'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[всё|Всё]] [[вы́глядит]] [[не]] '''о́чень'''.|Things don't look '''very good'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[звучи́т]] [[не]] '''о́чень'''.|That doesn't sound '''very good'''.}}

===References===
* {{R:ru:Vasmer}}
* {{cite-journal|author=Alexander Lehrman|title=The Etymology of OЧEНЬ|year=1987|journal=Russian Linguistics|volume=11|issue=1|pages=31-36}}

